{
  "opening": "This release introduces significant enhancements to the glom library, focusing on new specification types, improved CLI capabilities, and better debugging support through reprs. The following requirements define the observable behavior of the public API that must be present in the next release.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m15",
      "text": "The `glom_cli` command-line interface must accept Python-full specs rather than just AST literals, allowing for more complex specification definitions. When processing targets, it must correctly handle both AST literal targets and other formats via `mw_get_target` and `mw_handle_target`."
    },
    {
      "id": "m29",
      "text": "The library must expose the `Auto`, `Fill`, `Iter`, `Let`, and `ROOT` symbols as specified, ensuring they are accessible under these exact names. All public specifier types including `Check`, `First`, `GlomError`, `Glommer`, `Inspect`, `Spec`, `TType`, and functions like `all`, `chunked`, `dropwhile`, `fill`, `filter`, `first`, `flatten`, `glom`, and `glomit` must remain available and functional."
    },
    {
      "id": "m33",
      "text": "The `Invoke` class must provide a reasonable string representation (repr) for its expressions, particularly when used within nested scopes."
    },
    {
      "id": "m34",
      "text": "The `Invoke` class must expose a `constants` attribute instead of `consts`, ensuring backward compatibility or clear deprecation if `consts` is retained. Both `Invoke` and the module-level `constants` must be documented and accessible."
    },
    {
      "id": "m44",
      "text": "The `Fill` class must have a defined `__repr__` method that returns a readable string representation of the instance."
    },
    {
      "id": "m45",
      "text": "The `Assign` class and the `assign` function must have defined `__repr__` methods that return readable string representations of their instances."
    },
    {
      "id": "m46",
      "text": "The `Coalesce` class and the `Inspect` class must have defined `__repr__` methods that return readable string representations of their instances."
    },
    {
      "id": "m47",
      "text": "All public specifier types, including `Auto` and `Check`, must have reasonable `__repr__` implementations that clearly identify the spec type and its arguments."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please ensure all public names listed above are exposed exactly as specified and that the behavioral changes described are verified against the existing test suite."
}
